All,

Following is a brief on the CMF insurance and that provided by Harco.  The =
CMF insurance pitch is a misrepresentation of standard liability insurance =
that all credible businesses carry.  They frame their insurance in such a w=
ay that customers are caused to infer that installations errors (such as fu=
sion joints) will be covered by the product manufacturers.  In fact only ma=
nufacturing defects are covered.  All of our customers have always been cov=
ered by our liability insurance.

The CMF insurance is not licensed in Arizona, Connecticut, and Delaware.  D=
elaware is ironic because their insurance company is a business incorporate=
d in Delaware.

Summary:


Harco
CMF
Coverage including "umbrella"
$11m/$12m
$1m/$2m
Coverage by state guaranty fund
Yes
No
Coverage in all states
Yes
No
Covers fusion joint defects caused by contractor
No
No
Do suppliers "to" have liability insurance
Yes
Maybe (Menno???)
25 year warranty for manufacturing defects
Yes
Yes
Note:  It is a significant indicator that CMF's insurance is Non-Admitted v=
ersus Harco's insurance being Admitted.  Besides the coverage offered by a =
state guaranty fund that comes with Admitted insurance it is a measure of t=
he worthiness of CMF as a company.  Non-admitted insurance costs more than =
Admitted insurance and is insurance procured if a company cannot qualify fo=
r Admitted insurance.  Note the projects in Minneapolis require Admitted in=
surance.

Commentary:

Attached are CMF's and Harco's liability insurance certificates.

Harco's insurance is a superior insurance to CMF in that it is "Admitted" i=
n all states.  CMF's insurance operates on a "Non-Admitted" basis and is no=
t licensed in all states.

The Gemini Insurance Company (CMF's) operates on a non-admitted basis.  It =
is not operative in all states.  By operating on a non-admitted basis has a=
n effect on a claimant pursuing damages against an insured.  A non-admitted=
 carrier is defined as a company licensed or authorized to sell insurance t=
o the general public. In the United States, admitted companies are licensed=
 on a state-by-state basis and are differentiated from surplus lines insure=
rs, which are authorized to sell insurance in a state on a non-admitted bas=
is.  A non-admitted carrier is NOT subject to the provisions of a guaranty =
fund.  A guaranty fund is established by law in every state. Guaranty funds=
 are maintained by a state's insurance commissioner to protect policyholder=
s in the event that an insurer becomes insolvent or is unable to meet its f=
inancial obligations. The funds are usually financed by assessments against=
 all property and liability insurers regulated by a state.  Non-admitted in=
surance costs more and its use is usually a sign that the insured has certa=
in shortcomings in the view of the insurer.  The essence of the guaranty fu=
nd backing up insurance operating on an admitted basis is that the claimant=
 has more assured coverage.  In the case of the Minneapolis projects the li=
ability insurance is required to be "Admitted" in the state of Minnesota.

Harco's insurance is a superior insurance to CMF in that Harco has a $10m "=
umbrella" coverage that adds to the basic insurance.  CMF has $1m for each =
incident and $2m aggregate.  Harco has $11m for each incident and $12m aggr=
egate.

An umbrella policy is designed to provide protection against catastrophic l=
osses. It generally is written over various primary liability policies, suc=
h as the business auto policy (BAP), commercial general liability (CGL) pol=
icy, watercraft and aircraft liability policies, and employer's liability c=
overage. The umbrella policy serves three purposes: it provides excess limi=
ts when the limits of underlying liability policies are exhausted by the pa=
yment of claims; it drops down and picks up where the underlying policy lea=
ves off when the aggregate limit of the underlying policy in question is ex=
hausted by the payment of claims; and it provides protection against some c=
laims not covered by the underlying policies, subject to the assumption by =
the named insured of a self-insured retention (SIR).

Attached is CMF's flyer on their liability insurance.

The highlighted passages show that CMF's insurance offering provides only f=
or the case of a manufacturing defect and not for installation error.  CMF'=
s insurance simply calls on the insurance held by the source to CMF.  Note =
the passage in "Benefits to Club".  The coverage is from insurance companie=
s plural.  This is a reference to the insurances held by the different vend=
ors to CMF.  What liability insurance does Menno have?

The 25 year warranty against manufacturing defects that is an extension of =
the typical 1 year warranty is neither here nor there because in general a =
manufacturer would be held to account by a court of law for damages caused =
by manufacturing defects regardless of the stated term of the manufacturer'=
s warranty.  This is why all manufacturers readily extend their stated warr=
anty.

Please study this and develop the facility to use this information to dispu=
te and sell against CMF.

Advise us if you are not comfortable with using this information sell again=
st CMF.

J

